# =============================================================================
#
# CHAPTER 01
#
# INTRODUCTION
#
# =============================================================================

The COREI Knowledge System is the authoritative institutional knowledge
foundation of the COREI Operating System.

Its responsibility is not to store implementation.

Its responsibility is to organize institutional knowledge.

Every future knowledge asset shall follow this Knowledge System.

The objective is to ensure that COREI continues evolving without losing
institutional thinking, engineering knowledge, architectural reasoning,
or historical continuity.



# =============================================================================
#
# CHAPTER 02
#
# PURPOSE
#
# =============================================================================

The COREI Knowledge System exists to

• Preserve institutional knowledge.

• Organize knowledge consistently.

• Prevent knowledge duplication.

• Maintain a Single Source of Truth.

• Support engineering continuity.

• Support future engineering teams.

• Support AI-assisted reasoning.

• Improve discoverability.

• Ensure long-term scalability.

Knowledge is considered an institutional asset.

Documentation is one representation of that knowledge.



# =============================================================================
#
# CHAPTER 03
#
# KNOWLEDGE ARCHITECTURE
#
# =============================================================================

The COREI Knowledge System organizes all institutional knowledge into
permanent Knowledge Domains.

Every Knowledge Asset belongs to one primary Knowledge Domain.

Knowledge Domains remain stable regardless of

• Technology

• Programming Language

• Framework

• Repository

• Implementation

This allows COREI to evolve without reorganizing institutional knowledge.



# =============================================================================
#
# CHAPTER 04
#
# LEVEL-1 KNOWLEDGE DOMAINS
#
# =============================================================================

The COREI Knowledge System is organized into the following permanent
Knowledge Domains.

01 Identity

Defines who COREI is.

--------------------------------------------

02 Governance

Defines laws, principles, policies and governance.

--------------------------------------------

03 Architecture

Defines institutional architecture.

--------------------------------------------

04 Engineering

Defines engineering methodology.

--------------------------------------------

05 Standards

Defines reusable institutional standards.

--------------------------------------------

06 Specifications

Defines detailed technical specifications.

--------------------------------------------

07 Operations

Defines operational knowledge.

--------------------------------------------

08 Implementation

Defines implementation methodology.

--------------------------------------------

09 Reference

Defines glossary, taxonomy, indexes and references.

--------------------------------------------

10 History

Defines institutional evolution.

--------------------------------------------

11 Research

Defines investigations and exploratory knowledge.

These domains represent the highest level of institutional knowledge
classification within COREI.



# =============================================================================
#
# CHAPTER 05
#
# DOMAIN OWNERSHIP
#
# =============================================================================

Each Knowledge Domain owns a specific area of institutional knowledge.

Identity owns

• Identity

• Vision

• Mission

• Purpose

It does not own

• Architecture

• Implementation

--------------------------------------------

Governance owns

• Laws

• Principles

• Policies

It does not own

• Architecture Design

--------------------------------------------

Architecture owns

• Structural Design

• System Architecture

• Repository Architecture

It does not own

• Coding Standards

--------------------------------------------

Engineering owns

• Engineering Methodology

• Development Practices

It does not own

• Platform Architecture

...continues for all remaining Knowledge Domains...



# =============================================================================
#
# CHAPTER 06
#
# KNOWLEDGE CLASSIFICATION
#
# =============================================================================

Before creating a new Knowledge Asset,

the following questions shall always be answered.

Which Knowledge Domain owns this knowledge?

Does an authoritative Knowledge Asset already exist?

Does this duplicate existing knowledge?

Should this become a new Knowledge Asset
or belong to an existing one?

Knowledge shall always be classified before documentation begins.



# =============================================================================
#
# CHAPTER 07
#
# KNOWLEDGE LIFECYCLE
#
# =============================================================================

Every Knowledge Asset follows the same lifecycle.

Draft

↓

Review

↓

Approved

↓

Authoritative

↓

Frozen

↓

Superseded

↓

Archived

This lifecycle applies to every Knowledge Asset
within the COREI Knowledge System.



